          "source_sha256": "48a577b607243b0417e8a8032a350eb988790e53ad4a56f871e1a8ecaa495e74",
          "text": "## 5875afa30211\n\n**Reproduced defect \u2014 the advertised exact-axis contract is not callable or observable.**\n\nSource audited: generator v1.1.0, SHA-256 `48a577b607243b0417e8a8032a350eb988790e53ad4a56f871e1a8ecaa495e74`.\n\n`AXES` advertises `size=4..12` and `cell_count=1..30`, but `generate(123, 4, size=4, cell_count=1)` raises because the implementation silently narrows size to 6..9 in the default band; `size=12, cell_count=30` also raises. `palette_size=1` and `n_distinct_colors=1` are accepted but ignored: each call is byte-identical to the baseline and emits five nonzero colors. An unknown `typo_axis` is silently accepted and also returns the baseline grid. These are source-contract failures, so no Racket output is needed to reproduce them.\n\nEvidence and exact replay data are in `checks/audit/5875afa30211/finding.json`; `checks/audit/5875afa30211/reproduce.py` regenerates it. Suggested repair is to declare only meaningful controls, reject unknown keys, use strict typed draws with the full advertised domain in every band, and add `observe_overrides` for every exact axis.\n\nNo source change was made to this audit-only task.\n",
